# Temporary Scripts

When creating one-off, exploratory, or debugging scripts, write them to `packages/data/scripts/temp/` instead of `packages/data/scripts/`. The `packages/data/scripts/temp/` directory is gitignored and will not be committed.

Only scripts that are meant to be long-lived and re-run regularly should live in `packages/data/scripts/` directly. Write them as **TypeScript** (`.ts`) so `pnpm --filter @repo/data type-check` covers them. Run via `tsx scripts/<name>.ts` (see `packages/data/package.json`).

## Maintenance scripts (`pnpm --filter @repo/data …`)

| Script | Command |
|--------|---------|
| `build-pokemon-data-cache.ts` | `sync-api` |
| `enrich-michi-scene-art.ts` | `enrich-michi-scene-art` |
| `enrich-expensive-by-type.ts` | `enrich-expensive-by-type` |
| `enrich-competitive-snippet.ts` | `enrich-competitive` |
| `enrich-ability-descriptions.ts` | `enrich-abilities` |
| `generate-pokemon-facts.ts` | `generate-facts` |
| `audit-collection-tags.ts` | `audit-tags` |
| `backfill-artwork-urls.ts` | `backfill-artwork` |

## Shared libs (`scripts/lib/`)

- `cache-paths.ts` — package root + cache directory paths
- `pokemon-cache.ts` — read/write `cache/pokemon/*.json`
- `argv.ts` — `--limit`, `--only`, flags
- `artofpkm-scraper.ts` — artofpkm.com scene art scrape

Pokemon species metadata lives in committed `packages/data/cache/pokemon/` (not a separate catalog TS file).
